Design: the run console is one composed block

Steer #3 asks for composed surfaces, not a gallery: the run is the object
Stripe has no equivalent for, so this is the screen to win on.

RunConsole takes a run, its console totals and an optional prior total, and
renders the whole surface on the five-band widget anatomy — header (glyph,
period, status, provisional tag) · hero issued total with its delta chip ·
gauge that fills as items clear beside the lifecycle stepper and the metric
list · footer columns with a full-width CTA when there are exceptions.

Every reachable state is designed rather than absent: not-found, denied and
unavailable are their own frames; missing totals render em dashes; a run mid
issue carries the provisional tag; a measured zero exceptions reads "None"
because the em dash means unmeasured, not none.

Mounted on /runs/[id] in place of the disconnected metadata card + StatsGrid
the critique called out, catalogued as an L4 block in the gallery, and the
gallery's duplicate money-text case — a merge leftover that left the app lint
gate red — resolved to the single richer case.
EOF
