[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Design: the invoice shows the states Stripe cannot

Steer #3's opening is in-between states, and an invoice is where they live:
an enum says OPEN, the ledger says two payments landed and one is still in
flight, and the honest answer is "part paid · retrying".

InvoiceDetail derives part-paid, retrying, partially-refunded and past due
from the payment rows themselves and names each one in a sentence, then shows
those rows as evidence under the total — drill from a number to what produced
it. Footer carries the money triad: invoiced, collected, outstanding.

Outstanding needed arithmetic that did not exist, so lib/money.ts grows
sumMoney and subtractMoney, both on digit strings scaled to a common width:
no value meets a float, an unmeasured amount is skipped rather than folded in
as zero, and a balance with an unmeasured term is unmeasured instead of
confidently re-invoicing money that already arrived. Five tests, including
0.1 + 0.2 and the cent case.

Mounted on /invoices/[id] in place of the metadata card, and catalogued in
the gallery alongside the run console with all four states rendered.
EOF
